    "evidence": [
      "Authorize one coherent network-interface source owner for the existing fourteen public synch_* notification operations and network-aware wait_2 bridge, plus the complete current NetDaemon implementation/caller closure. Header declarations are already shared across real game/UI owners; original BaseWin zoom calls wait_2, whose original branches tail-call net_tasks or Win wait_task. No historical TU identity is asserted.",
      "One capped immutable native production-recipe family diagnostic at9c2b87174 preserves all14 exact notification bodies and restores wait_2 to6/6 instructions with no prior exact loss. Baseline replay, unchanged-object replica and a compiled branch-inversion damage control pass. This is only diagnostic evidence; source/build/link and whole-census verification remain required.",
      "Move complete unchanged C++ bodies, ORIGINAL envelopes and useful prose to src/netdaemon_interface.cpp. Keep NetDaemonNet, NetBusyCount, IsMultiplayerNet, Spock flags and all genuine storage in existing owners. New TU uses existing declarations and the same NetDaemon /Oy- source profile. No flags, noinline/export, assembly/copied bytes, wrappers, casts, original-address dispatch, behavior fixes or signature/layout changes.",
      "Update actual-source and strict inverse readers for the exact transport. Add host/damage controls for both network-aware wait branches and every notification opcode/argument contract. Preserve immutable historical baselines and visible preexisting failures; do not substitute baseline bodies or add wildcards/waivers. Correct stale source-owner comments, including wait_task original5FC700 (already the bound real Win pump) and the obsolete claim that real NetDaemon::synch is an original-address dependency.",
      "Manual integration requires original/source review, fresh full build/link, complete identity/span/claim/lesson continuity, whole matching census with no unexplained outside losses, physical outside-object replicas, and independent review plus fresh destination recheck. Existing full linked/structure/runtime/automatic/game acceptance remains unproven. Task baseline is immutable."
    ],
